; SetupVarGUI batch config file.
; Place this next to SetupVarGUI.efi (or BOOTX64.EFI) as "setupvar.cfg"
; and pick "Load & apply config file" from the main menu.
;
; Format (one entry per line):
;   VarStoreName:0xOFFSET(SIZE)=0xVALUE ; free-text description
;
; VarStoreName  - NVRAM variable name, usually "Setup" (some Insyde
;                 firmwares use "Custom" or an OEM-specific name)
; OFFSET        - hex byte offset into that variable's data
; SIZE          - value size in bytes: 1, 2 or 4 (defaults to 1)
; VALUE         - hex value to write
;
; You must determine the correct offsets for YOUR exact firmware
; version yourself (e.g. via IFR extraction tools such as
; Universal-IFR-Extractor). Offsets are NOT portable between
; motherboards or even BIOS versions of the same board.
;
; Lines starting with ';' or '#' are comments and are ignored.

; --- examples only, DO NOT use on real hardware without verifying ---
; Setup:0x0CA9(1)=0x01 ; Intel C-State -> Enabled
; Setup:0x058D(1)=0x00 ; Overclocking Lock -> Unlocked
